{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2288","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2288","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2288\",\"parent_revision\":\"40867746e75d66452b5083112ce4f6748d221da828df08f60969c2ea06a9243f\",\"root_revision\":\"40867746e75d66452b5083112ce4f6748d221da828df08f60969c2ea06a9243f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe architect spec \u00a74.1 line 214 requires BdRunner.__init__ to accept an env_overrides parameter: `__init__(*, env_overrides: Mapping[str, str] | None = None, timeout_seconds: int = _DEFAULT_BD_TIMEOUT_SECONDS)`. The implementation at plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/bd_runner.py:146 only has `timeout_seconds` \u2014 env_overrides is absent. This makes it impossible for callers to override subprocess environment variables without modifying the class.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **bdrunner.__init__ missing env_overrides parameter required by spec** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality vigilance concern from #2279 \u2014 contract-verification agent on T05, confirmed by grep of bd_runner.py:146\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-15\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:6b3ec6e952a296616d042b0e16ad28c7 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-21)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `BdRunner.__init__` accepts `env_overrides: Mapping[str, str] | None = None` as keyword-only parameter\\n- `env_overrides` values are merged into subprocess environment in both `_run()` and `is_available()`\\n- `env_overrides=None` behavior is identical to current behavior\\n- Tests added covering env_overrides merge and None behavior\\n\\n### Description\\n\\nAdd `env_overrides: Mapping[str, str] | None = None` keyword-only parameter to `BdRunner.__init__` per architect spec \u00a74.1 line 214. Store as `self._env_overrides`. Merge into subprocess env dict in `_run()` and `is_available()` by updating `_bd_env()` calls to use a merged dict with env_overrides taking precedence.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\nSingle file: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/bd_runner.py`. Parameter change is additive \u2014 all callers use keyword args or no args. No callers pass `timeout_seconds` positionally.\\n\",\"digest\":\"4c9461a80028fa1beb7bbd7fac8882d7dcc262c89c83e411f19d306073321cff\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCRM2Q\"}"}